{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "003S", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$p : G \\to H$", "MATH_0002": "$p : \\mathcal{S}\\to\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$p : \\mathcal{S}\\to\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$p$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{S}_U$", "MATH_0006": "$U\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0007": "$p$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-group-homomorphism-functor}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{example-group-groupoid}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-group-homomorphism-fibreedingroupoids}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d98e7db592445511bdddc2318034a393b2dec6a74a62eb6e86efa2853d197b9e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:656f9c20bf4d1b3dfae4d689f0a01640f9b471720625a22d24ebc9b3bbfe8b18", "source_text": "A homomorphism of groups <MATH_0001> gives rise to a functor\n<MATH_0002> as in Example\n<REF_0001>. This functor\n<MATH_0003> is fibred in groupoids if and only if\n<MATH_0004> is surjective. The fibre category <MATH_0005> over the (unique)\nobject <MATH_0006> is the category associated to the\nkernel of <MATH_0007> as in Example <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3adee198f98bd773388f1536e0bf961029d26c1ef044d64279832f84d9faae82", "unit_id": "tag:003U:statement"}
